      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "No, smart building systems cannot be programmed to intentionally emit specific infrasound frequencies to cause physical sensations like chest pressure or regulate human behavior through crowd control. The mechanics and cost of retrofitting such equipment into existing HVAC infrastructure would be prohibitively expensive and technically complex for standard occupancy buildings. While legitimate psychological confusion can occur under certain conditions, the idea that a HVAC system is targeting individual frequencies to manipulate consciousness is not supported by current technology or scientific evidence.",
